// Plan stage R0z Z9c-B (R-VREF, review round 2, B3 and B4; the ok twin):
// a reference can be live in the window of the task, so the call keeps the
// rule of main. The probe of the review:
// Review probe Z9c-B r2 (R-VREF edge): as q19, `par` holds a value of a type parameter (a reference into `w`)
// and gives it back to `show` after the call; one value of the interface `h` and one generic value.
fn par<T>(h: fn(), x: T, show: fn(T)) / async {
    let f = || scope { s => s.spawn(h); () }
    let y = x
    f()
    show(y)
}
fn main() / async {
    let w = Vec.new()
    w.push(1)
    par(|| print(w.len()), &w[0], |y: &u64| print(y))
}
